# Upstream's own ignore conventions, kept verbatim. Nothing above this line is
# ours, and nothing below it removes an upstream entry to make room for a
# fork-owned one.
#
# simdjson's release tarball ships no `.gitignore` at all, so the first block is
# this fork's reading of what upstream's *build system* produces rather than a
# copy of an upstream file. The entries come from upstream's own CMake
# definitions: `src/CMakeLists.txt:204` is the single source file
# `src/src/simdjson.cpp`, and every object and archive in a CMake build is
# derived from it, so `*.o`, `*.a` and `*.obj` are the outputs a build leaves in
# the source tree. The Windows entries are there because upstream's CMake has
# real Windows and MSVC targets: `src/windows/` carries the mingw-w64 and NetBSD
# derived files its build uses, and `src/CMakeLists.txt:256` sets
# `WINDOWS_EXPORT_ALL_SYMBOLS YES`, so a Windows build produces a `.dll`, an
# import `.lib` and a `.exp`. None of them is produced by this package's Zig
# graph, which builds with `zig build` and installs to `--prefix` -- they are
# listed so a `cmake` run left in the tree cannot be committed into a tree that is
# built with Zig instead.
*.o
*.a
*.so
*.so.*
*.obj
*.lib
*.exp
*.pdb
*.ilk
*.dll
*.exe
*.manifest
*.dmp
*.swp

# The amalgamated single-header output, ignored even though the three files it
# would produce are deliberately absent from `src/` (see UPSTREAM.md). This is a
# belt-and-braces entry: `tools/check-provenance.sh` fails if they reappear, and
# this stops a build from staging one before the gate runs.
src/singleheader/simdjson.h
src/singleheader/simdjson.cpp
src/singleheader/singleheader.zip

# zig build artefacts (fork addition).
#
# These are directories rather than single files because a normal `zig build`
# creates them, and a normal `zig build` must not dirty the tree or leak into the
# package published from it. None of them is named in build.zig.zon `.paths`, so
# an ignored directory can never become part of the package.
.zig-cache/
zig-out/
# Zig 0.16 fetches dependencies into a project-local directory. This package
# declares no dependencies, so this exists only so that a future one cannot
# commit a fetched tree.
zig-pkg/

# The consumer package builds inside this repository and has its own cache and
# output tree. It is ignored here as well as in consumer/.gitignore so a build
# run from the repository root cannot commit it by accident.
consumer/.zig-cache/
consumer/zig-out/
consumer/zig-pkg/

# Nix and devenv working-tree artefacts (fork addition).
#
# `nix build` writes `result` (and `result-1`, `result-2`, ... on a rebuild)
# into the directory that asked for it, and `devenv` writes its resolved inputs
# and its state beside the project. None of them is named in build.zig.zon
# `.paths`, so an ignored path can never become part of the package either.
# `devenv.lock` and `flake.lock` are deliberately *not* here: they are real
# inputs, they belong to the driver, and ignoring them would be the wrong way to
# keep a build out of a commit.
result
result-*
.devenv/
.devenv.flake.nix
.devenv.flakes/
devenv.local.nix
.direnv/